   "definitions": [
    {
     "definition": "A family of genes that encode a subfamily of RNA binding proteins that have a shared structure, which contains a transcriptional-activation domain (TEAD), three regions that are rich in arginine and glycine (RGG), an RNA recognition motif (RRM), and a RanBP2 (C2C2)-type zinc finger domain. They are involved in transcription regulation, RNA splicing, RNA transport, DNA damage response and DNA repair.",
